cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LR-AI in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "LR-AI: Automated literature reviews with Claude Code"
type: software
abstract: >-
  LR-AI is an open-source Claude Code plugin that automates the search and screening stages of a literature
  review. It runs seed searches and boolean database searches on OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar and arXiv, snowballs
  forward and backward through citations, de-duplicates and filters the results, screens every paper with
  parallel subagents, builds a taxonomy with summaries, and exports a categorized Google Sheet or Excel workbook
  with a PRISMA-style methods tab.
version: 0.2.7
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YAZANGTHB/lr-ai"
url: "https://github.com/YAZANGTHB/lr-ai"
authors:
  - family-names: Alnakri
    given-names: Yazan
keywords:
  - literature review
  - systematic review
  - snowballing
  - research automation
